A quick google finds TVs are actually 640x480.

The reason TVs aren't good at showing text is that the resolution is so 
low. You'd have the same problems showing text on a 30" low-res computer 
monitor: The text has to be huge to be readable.

However, for NetHack, the screen resolution is about 640x300 (80x25 for 
8x12 characters is pretty standard, I think). You can show it on a TV 
without too much trouble, especially if you don't stretch it.

TVs also have a bit of extra fuzziness besides low resolution, but the 
resolution is the main thing. Nethack can handle some fuzziness anyway.

